# Qwen Polyglot AST Cartographer (`qwen-polyglot-ast-cartographer`)

Alibaba Qwen 2.5 Coder excels at rapid repository indexing by constructing lightweight **Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) maps**: extracting class hierarchies, function signatures, and exported interfaces without loading full function bodies or comments.

This skill equips Gemini with Qwen-style AST cartography, allowing Argon to understand 10,000 lines of multi-language code using under 500 tokens.

---

## 1. High-Density Symbol Notation

### Raw File (250 lines / ~1,200 tokens):
Loading full C++ or Lua implementations into context.

### Qwen-Style Symbol Skeleton (Compact: 45 tokens — 96% reduction):
```text
[AST_MAP: xrGame/weapon.h]
class CWeapon : public CHudItem, public CPhysicsShellHolder {
  + virtual void Fire() -> void
  + virtual void Reload() -> void
  + virtual bool CanAttach(CInventoryItem*) const -> bool
  # u32 m_cost; float m_weight;
}
```

---

## 2. Extraction Commands

Extract symbol outlines instantly using local host tools:

```bash
# Extract C++ class and method signatures via ctags/tree-sitter/grep
ctags -x --c++-kinds=c+m src/weapons/weapon.cpp | head -n 30

# Extract Python function signatures without function bodies
python3 -c '
import ast, sys
tree = ast.parse(open("tools/save_fps.py").read())
for node in ast.walk(tree):
    if isinstance(node, (ast.FunctionDef, ast.ClassDef)):
        print(f"{type(node).__name__}: {node.name}")
'
```
